{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>לב צדיק</b> — he thinks to answer with just judgment." "<b>יביע</b> — like נובע (flowing). The meaning: he speaks evil things in order to pervert judgment; therefore HaShem is far from them, but He hears the prayer of the righteous." "Another interpretation: לענות — from לענה (wormwood) and ראש (gall), but this is far-fetched, because the lamed does not have a sheva."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:04.736443972Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}